Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.26,0:00:15.40,Default,,0,0,0,,This place is...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.48,0:00:18.06,Default,,0,0,0,,this place is Green Dolphin\NStreet State Prison!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.14,0:00:19.12,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.20,0:00:21.85,Default,,0,0,0,,in the hallway in front\Nof the visiting room!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.60,0:00:25.13,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell do you want?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.32,0:00:27.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't want to see your face.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.28,0:00:29.92,Default,,0,0,0,,You think you can just come\Nwaltzing back into my life?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.00,0:00:32.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't show up acting all fatherly now!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.84,0:00:34.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to help you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.96,0:00:37.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna get you out of here soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.92,0:00:38.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, shut up!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.22,0:00:42.75,Default,,0,0,0,,You know damn well you\Ncan't pull that off.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.90,0:00:44.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Two years for a hit and run is nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.94,0:00:46.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I can handle it fine by myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.14,0:00:47.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Just relax.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.26,0:00:50.40,Default,,0,0,0,,For the longest time, I've wanted to...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.48,0:00:51.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Keep that shit to yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.96,0:00:54.76,Default,,0,0,0,,The last thing I need is for you\Nto try acting like a real father.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.84,0:00:55.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Go away!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.48,0:00:59.31,Default,,0,0,0,,What the...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.39,0:01:00.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Who are these two?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.40,0:01:03.93,Default,,0,0,0,,These people look so\Nsimilar to the others.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.56,0:01:05.64,Default,,0,0,0,,But they're not.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.86,0:01:07.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Get lost already!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.28,0:01:09.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't get along with you, remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.86,0:01:12.28,Default,,0,0,0,,What is going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.54,0:01:15.13,Default,,0,0,0,,We were just in Cape\NCanaveral a minute ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.62,0:01:18.34,Default,,0,0,0,,And also, for that matter...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.42,0:01:20.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Just when the heck is it right now?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.02,0:01:23.96,Default,,0,0,0,,It is November 30th, in the year 2011.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.02,0:01:39.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Who the hell are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.54,0:01:42.16,Default,,0,0,0,,During visitation, not\Neven a priest can...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.78,0:01:46.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you say 2011?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.82,0:01:48.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Does that mean we went back in time?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.78,0:01:50.02,Default,,0,0,0,,No, actually.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.46,0:01:52.76,Default,,0,0,0,,We have traveled far beyond that point.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.40,0:01:57.34,Default,,0,0,0,,With accelerated time, we've reached\Na place humanity always winds up.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.42,0:01:58.83,Default,,0,0,0,,The end of the universe!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.86,0:02:04.51,Default,,0,0,0,,As in life, the ending of something\Ninitiates a new beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.80,0:02:06.82,Default,,0,0,0,,And that is what we call fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.08,0:02:08.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Even in the universe after this,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.12,0:02:11.58,Default,,0,0,0,,our planet will be\Nrecreated and life on Earth
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.66,0:02:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,will follow the same path\Nthat it was destined to.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.26,0:02:18.60,Default,,0,0,0,,And when humanity comes into existence,\Nit will be the beginning of a new dawn.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.68,0:02:22.64,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the promised age of happiness\Nbrought forth by Maiden Heaven.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.72,0:02:25.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Bear witness to the new world!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.58,0:02:27.41,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.49,0:02:28.49,Default,,0,0,0,,What is he even saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.58,0:02:32.56,Default,,0,0,0,,In this new world, the Jolyne\NCujo you knew exists no longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.04,0:02:35.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Neither do Jotaro, Anastasia, nor Hermes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.88,0:02:38.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Not even their souls\Nsurvive total annihilation.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.38,0:02:41.91,Default,,0,0,0,,And that is because\Nthe dead cannot return.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.26,0:02:46.55,Default,,0,0,0,,All of those who perish in the\Naccelerated time have been erased forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.72,0:02:51.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I left everyone who ever dared to interfere\Nwith my destiny back in the other world.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.66,0:02:54.40,Default,,0,0,0,,All of them except for you, Emporio!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.02,0:02:58.14,Default,,0,0,0,,You were never supposed to\Nexist in this new reality!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.58,0:03:01.99,Default,,0,0,0,,So now I'm left with no other\Nchoice but to eliminate you!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.16,0:03:07.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Destiny is mine!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.60,0:03:11.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid that all of the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.58,0:03:14.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not afraid of
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.12,0:03:19.98,Default,,0,0,0,,sugar's rain of lies.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.74,0:03:26.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Itaami o no
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.10,0:03:29.66,Default,,0,0,0,,eko elu tabi.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.74,0:03:34.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Kokoro wa eilu ni
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.22,0:03:38.56,Default,,0,0,0,,togi Zoom sareru.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.64,0:03:43.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Cairo kae Zero Seiko
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.00,0:03:47.16,Default,,0,0,0,,mei no sai hate ne?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.90,0:03:53.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.16,0:04:17.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is life?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.38,0:04:19.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Wie if it is?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.26,0:04:22.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Siege it with the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.64,0:04:23.86,Default,,0,0,0,,It's something that you can't do.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.94,0:04:28.70,Default,,0,0,0,,It's something that you can't do.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.78,0:04:29.92,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.86,0:04:31.69,Default,,0,0,0,,No, no, no, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.77,0:04:35.82,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.84,0:04:44.84,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.92,0:04:46.18,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.26,0:04:47.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Code 909.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.92,0:04:48.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Security level 4.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.02,0:04:50.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Emergency alarm in the visiting room.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.88,0:04:51.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Inner door.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.79,0:04:52.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Code 909.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.82,0:04:53.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Security level 4.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.96,0:04:54.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Emergency alarm in the visiting room.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.06,0:04:55.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Inner door.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.97,0:04:56.80,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.89,0:04:57.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Dunno, but now's our chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.80,0:04:58.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's bounce!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.66,0:05:01.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene broke out of prison last time too!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.96,0:05:04.80,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, it's the same but different!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.40,0:05:06.66,Default,,0,0,0,,That's fate at work.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.96,0:05:10.08,Default,,0,0,0,,This new universe has reached\Nthis point in time after
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.16,0:05:12.48,Default,,0,0,0,,repeating the same history\Nas the previous universe,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.56,0:05:14.02,Default,,0,0,0,,and it shall be the same Haruno.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.10,0:05:19.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Because that is fate, and fate is brought\Non by certainty, not by coincidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.98,0:05:24.45,Default,,0,0,0,,For instance, your next move will be\Nto escape and try to hide in your room.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.90,0:05:28.67,Default,,0,0,0,,The very same room you used to\Nhide in in the previous universe.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.76,0:05:30.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Your secret room, as it was called.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.44,0:05:36.44,Default,,0,0,0,,The fact that you're going to retreat\Nhere had already been decided.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.46,0:05:43.60,Default,,0,0,0,,It's no use!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.10,0:05:46.22,Default,,0,0,0,,to find somewhere other\Nthan my room to hide!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.30,0:05:49.46,Default,,0,0,0,,How on earth did the prisoners\Nwind up in the common area?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.54,0:05:51.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Hell if I know, just move your ass!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.40,0:05:53.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Those guards are from before.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.12,0:05:55.24,Default,,0,0,0,,They're gonna fall.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.38,0:05:57.21,Default,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.70,0:05:58.72,Default,,0,0,0,,We're gonna fall.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.64,0:06:04.58,Default,,0,0,0,,If we keep going at this pace, we're\Ngonna end up having a nasty fall.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.66,0:06:05.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.57,0:06:07.34,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.74,0:06:11.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, uh, it just kinda came to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.28,0:06:14.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not sure why, but it feels\Nlike we're gonna fall somehow.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.36,0:06:15.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't tell me you're afraid!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.90,0:06:16.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Now get moving!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.81,0:06:17.92,Default,,0,0,0,,You want a pay cut?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.36,0:06:19.19,Default,,0,0,0,,How come?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.70,0:06:21.29,Default,,0,0,0,,For some reason I know too.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.90,0:06:24.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Both of those guards are going to...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.58,0:06:33.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Father, hi!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.14,0:06:34.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Can I help you?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.05,0:06:35.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Move it!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.60,0:06:41.12,Default,,0,0,0,,There's not a soul in this world!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.20,0:06:42.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Can escape their fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.42,0:06:45.13,Default,,0,0,0,,You most certainly will\Nbe going to that room.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.24,0:06:55.26,Default,,0,0,0,,What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.34,0:06:56.58,Default,,0,0,0,,What the heck is going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.66,0:07:00.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Right now we have traveled\Nfar beyond that point.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.18,0:07:02.58,Default,,0,0,0,,With accelerated time\Nwe have reached a place
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.66,0:07:06.36,Default,,0,0,0,,humanity always winds\Nup the ultimate end of.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.98,0:07:07.81,Default,,0,0,0,,universe.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.89,0:07:08.85,Default,,0,0,0,,The end of the universe.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.24,0:07:12.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I remember reading about that\Nsomewhere, in a book on the
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.34,0:07:15.62,Default,,0,0,0,,beginning and end of all things.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.70,0:07:17.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Since the dawn of creation,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.52,0:07:20.36,Default,,0,0,0,,the universe continues to\Nexpand, but at one point,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.44,0:07:24.90,Default,,0,0,0,,it starts to contract, almost as if you\Nare tightly squeezing a sponge ball.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.98,0:07:28.80,Default,,0,0,0,,When it can no longer contract, the\Nuniverse reaches its singularity point.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.88,0:07:32.36,Default,,0,0,0,,But there is a theory that the\NBig Bang will repeat itself,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.54,0:07:35.66,Default,,0,0,0,,and a new universe will be\Ncreated to replace the old
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.86,0:07:39.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Does this mean that we traveled\Nhere from the previous world?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.16,0:07:42.56,Default,,0,0,0,,We made it all the way to the new 2011,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.88,0:07:45.74,Default,,0,0,0,,and at a tremendous speed\Nwe journeyed through time as
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.82,0:07:49.11,Default,,0,0,0,,the Earth progressed and\Nevolved at the same rapid pace.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.54,0:07:52.02,Default,,0,0,0,,But not everyone made the journey with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.50,0:07:54.79,Default,,0,0,0,,That is because the dead cannot return,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.06,0:07:59.71,Default,,0,0,0,,and all of those who perished in the\Naccelerated time have been erased forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.38,0:08:04.72,Default,,0,0,0,,They're not here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.14,0:08:09.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene and everyone else, they're gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.70,0:08:21.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm all alone, again.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.64,0:08:27.06,Default,,0,0,0,,The fortunate souls who were able to\Ntranscend time have been blessed. No!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.64,0:08:31.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Those members of the human\Nrace who survived have
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.16,0:08:34.18,Default,,0,0,0,,experienced the future and\Narrived at this new world.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.26,0:08:38.48,Default,,0,0,0,,The one truth of this universe is\Nthat fate will always take its course.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.56,0:08:41.00,Default,,0,0,0,,And in turn, destiny will repeat itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.42,0:08:44.56,Default,,0,0,0,,When one human being meets\Nanother, it is due to gravity.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.64,0:08:47.50,Default,,0,0,0,,They come together because\Nit was fated to be that way.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.58,0:08:50.93,Default,,0,0,0,,For example, what events will\Nunfold five years from now?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.20,0:08:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to their travels\Nthrough the accelerated time,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.98,0:08:57.08,Default,,0,0,0,,humanity has already experienced it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.16,0:08:59.36,Default,,0,0,0,,They already know when\Nthey'll get into an accident,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.44,0:09:01.50,Default,,0,0,0,,when they'll succumb to an illness,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.64,0:09:04.29,Default,,0,0,0,,and even when their life\Nwill come to an end.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.12,0:09:07.42,Default,,0,0,0,,When will they meet and part with another?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.50,0:09:12.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Who will they fall in love with, and who\Nwill they hate with a burning passion?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.20,0:09:16.40,Default,,0,0,0,,How many children will one bear, and what\Nkind of people will those children become?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.48,0:09:21.04,Default,,0,0,0,,When will war be declared, and when\Nwill the world undergo a change?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.64,0:09:25.48,Default,,0,0,0,,They experience it as though\Nthey're watching a movie.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.56,0:09:29.62,Default,,0,0,0,,So too will their children, and even\Nthe generation that comes after.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.88,0:09:33.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Back in Cape Canaveral\Nis where it all began.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.94,0:09:35.48,Default,,0,0,0,,All of those who live through accelerated
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.56,0:09:37.58,Default,,0,0,0,,time are aware of everything\Nthat shall happen,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.66,0:09:39.72,Default,,0,0,0,,not because they saw it and memorized it,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.80,0:09:42.74,Default,,0,0,0,,but because it has been\Nengraved into their minds!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.96,0:09:46.42,Default,,0,0,0,,And that is how this world\Nwill know true happiness
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.50,0:09:49.46,Default,,0,0,0,,because they can be resolute\Nto face their future.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.34,0:09:53.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The ones who find this\Nresolve shall be truly happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.08,0:09:55.42,Default,,0,0,0,,You may think to yourself\Nwhy would I want to
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.50,0:09:57.94,Default,,0,0,0,,know this would it not\Njust bring me despair?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.02,0:09:59.30,Default,,0,0,0,,But you're wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.38,0:10:03.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if you knew that tomorrow was\Nyour last day being prepared allows you
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.82,0:10:08.10,Default,,0,0,0,,to go in peace because one's resolution\Nwill eradicate all of that despair.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.18,0:10:10.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Humanity will be changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.66,0:10:12.54,Default,,0,0,0,,This is what we strove for.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.62,0:10:16.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Dio and I fought tirelessly to attain\Nheaven and now we're finally here.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.68,0:10:19.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Made in heaven is the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.84,0:10:24.67,Default,,0,0,0,,My gun.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.75,0:10:25.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.78,0:10:27.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.20,0:10:28.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I dropped it in the ocean.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.00,0:10:32.46,Default,,0,0,0,,If I might go right at the corner.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.54,0:10:35.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll come to a set of stairs and that's\Nwhere my ghost This room should be,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.06,0:10:37.40,Default,,0,0,0,,but Poochie already knows.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.48,0:10:38.66,Default,,0,0,0,,all about that room.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.98,0:10:40.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I need to go the other way.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.84,0:10:44.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Turn left, if I go this way\NI can hide somewhere else.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.24,0:11:03.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if the smallest of\Ndetails might go astray,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.00,0:11:06.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Defeating fate is simply impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.26,0:11:11.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Your only option now is running\Naway into your crack in the wall.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.64,0:11:19.06,Default,,0,0,0,,If I let you get away from me here,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.36,0:11:21.38,Default,,0,0,0,,and I end up losing track of you,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.60,0:11:24.66,Default,,0,0,0,,then you will most likely\Ntry to defeat me later on.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.88,0:11:27.54,Default,,0,0,0,,That is the future that\Nis destined to happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.62,0:11:30.44,Default,,0,0,0,,So unfortunately for you,\NI cannot let you live.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.86,0:11:32.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Even without the help of\NJolene and the others,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.78,0:11:34.90,Default,,0,0,0,,it is your fate to break\Nfree from this prison,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.98,0:11:38.80,Default,,0,0,0,,as it is still my destiny to lose\Nsight of you at Cape Canaveral.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.18,0:11:41.32,Default,,0,0,0,,The reason I chose to\Nbring us here is because
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.40,0:11:44.02,Default,,0,0,0,,it's before I sped up\Ntime in Cape Canaveral.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.10,0:11:46.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Here I knew I could find\Nexactly where you were hiding.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.40,0:11:50.44,Default,,0,0,0,,The only chance I have to eliminate\Nyou for good is right here and now.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.52,0:11:52.24,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why I elected\Nto stop the passing of
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.32,0:11:54.32,Default,,0,0,0,,time at the moment you\Nwere most vulnerable.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.40,0:11:56.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Now prepare yourself to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.36,0:11:59.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Only by accepting your death\Ncan you be happy, Emporio.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.56,0:12:07.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Your only hope!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.22,0:12:14.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I do this now for the\Nsake of all humanity!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.86,0:12:16.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Die, Encario!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.94,0:12:32.98,Default,,0,0,0,,You see, fate is predetermined.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.08,0:12:34.26,Default,,0,0,0,,It can't be changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.74,0:12:39.22,Default,,0,0,0,,If that's true, then I'll just\Nhave to make you change it for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.30,0:12:43.36,Default,,0,0,0,,When we were entering through\Nthe crack in the wall,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.58,0:12:45.58,Default,,0,0,0,,your arm pushed this into my head.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.44,0:12:50.30,Default,,0,0,0,,In the final moments before\NWeatherforecast died,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.38,0:12:53.56,Default,,0,0,0,,he turned a stand ability into a disc\Nbefore you landed the final blow.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.64,0:12:56.80,Default,,0,0,0,,And it's the same disc that\NJolene decided to entrust to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.88,0:12:59.65,Default,,0,0,0,,So I've been holding on\Nto it for both of them!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.98,0:13:09.98,Default,,0,0,0,,In the name of God, I will\Ndestroy you. Your actions
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.06,0:13:12.90,Default,,0,0,0,,here today Emporio all\Nthey have accomplished
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.98,0:13:14.78,Default,,0,0,0,,is Solidifying the fact\Nthat your screams will
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.86,0:13:17.94,Default,,0,0,0,,become the trumpets of\Nhell even if you insert
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.02,0:13:19.88,Default,,0,0,0,,someone Else's disc into\Nthat mindless head of
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.96,0:13:22.02,Default,,0,0,0,,yours whether's ability\Nis what it is because
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.10,0:13:25.40,Default,,0,0,0,,of his Own talent do not\Narrogantly assume that
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.48,0:13:28.19,Default,,0,0,0,,you can just feel that\Nkind of power so easily
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.36,0:13:34.90,Default,,0,0,0,,And besides, to stop you, I've\Naccelerated time once more!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.36,0:13:38.50,Default,,0,0,0,,In front of my honorable\Nambitions, Emporio,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.06,0:13:43.65,Default,,0,0,0,,you shall come to realize your own\Ninsignificance as you wither and fade away!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.88,0:14:08.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Very helpful Assistant
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.24,0:14:12.40,Default,,0,0,0,,something is wrong what is this madness
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.82,0:14:18.38,Default,,0,0,0,,It's weather forecast. One day I
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.46,0:14:20.92,Default,,0,0,0,,read in a book that the deadliest
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.00,0:14:24.62,Default,,0,0,0,,poison within proximity of any\Norganism is the air they breathe.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.70,0:14:27.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Every organism on this planet\Nneeds oxygen to survive,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.04,0:14:31.80,Default,,0,0,0,,but the concentration level\Nof oxygen can't be above 40%.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.30,0:14:37.42,Default,,0,0,0,,100 % pure oxygen is extremely toxic, and\Nany life form exposed to it will perish.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.90,0:14:41.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Highly concentrated levels of oxygen\Ncan corrode iron in a matter of seconds,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.86,0:14:43.45,Default,,0,0,0,,and even make fire explode.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.70,0:14:46.22,Default,,0,0,0,,It can also absorb\Nelectrons in the human body,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.30,0:14:49.34,Default,,0,0,0,,slowly destroying the cell\Ntissues one after another.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.42,0:14:53.14,Default,,0,0,0,,If you breathe too much of it, Your\Nhands and feet will start to go numb?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.22,0:14:54.88,Default,,0,0,0,,and you won't be able to stand.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.96,0:14:58.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Plus, the tiny veins in your eyes\Nwill snap and you'll go blind.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.16,0:15:01.10,Default,,0,0,0,,You can go ahead and\Naccelerate time all you want.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.22,0:15:04.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Weather forecast is a stand\Nthat can control the weather.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.40,0:15:08.60,Default,,0,0,0,,I already used it to accumulate a massive\Namount of pure oxygen into this room.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.68,0:15:11.15,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, you'll slowly lose consciousness,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.26,0:15:14.74,Default,,0,0,0,,as 100 % oxygen seeps deeper\Nand deeper into your tissues.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.44,0:15:18.34,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I refuse to let a\Nbranch like you beat me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.66,0:15:20.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not the one in control here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.62,0:15:23.09,Default,,0,0,0,,This is Weather Forecast's hidden ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.64,0:15:25.34,Default,,0,0,0,,You're the one who stole Weather's memory?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.42,0:15:26.92,Default,,0,0,0,,and the one who awakened him again!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.00,0:15:30.06,Default,,0,0,0,,when he regained his power\Nto project killer snails.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.16,0:15:33.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Father Poochie, it was all because of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.12,0:15:36.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Gravity still affects you, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.68,0:15:39.02,Default,,0,0,0,,You are unable to defeat your destiny.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.18,0:15:44.88,Default,,0,0,0,,No, you have to end this, Empirical.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.10,0:15:46.68,Default,,0,0,0,,You can still stop Weather.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.76,0:15:48.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Do not let him do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.56,0:15:52.26,Default,,0,0,0,,After I finally attained the\Nability, I've worked so hard for.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.46,0:15:54.00,Default,,0,0,0,,God wished it to be so!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.24,0:15:57.24,Default,,0,0,0,,It was an ability that God\Nchose for me to possess!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.48,0:16:02.19,Default,,0,0,0,,A new history of humanity will be born,\Nand the future of mankind will be saved!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.46,0:16:04.52,Default,,0,0,0,,We haven't even reached\Nthe point in time yet
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.60,0:16:07.54,Default,,0,0,0,,where time acceleration\Nstarted in Cape Canaveral.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.82,0:16:10.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Maiden Heaven has yet to be completed.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.34,0:16:14.36,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as it's after Cape Canaveral,\NI will gladly sacrifice my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.44,0:16:15.68,Default,,0,0,0,,But if I die now,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.90,0:16:19.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't mean that everything I've done thus\Nfar will have been utterly meaningless.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.72,0:16:22.60,Default,,0,0,0,,The fate of all humanity\Nwill be changed forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.74,0:16:27.04,Default,,0,0,0,,If i die, people won't be able to see\Ntheir future as it happens before them?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.12,0:16:29.50,Default,,0,0,0,,which means they won't be\Nable to face their fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.58,0:16:30.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.88,0:16:33.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Accepting their fate is\Nhow they'll be truly happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.50,0:16:36.00,Default,,0,0,0,,It was my mission to bring\Nabout true happiness.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.08,0:16:37.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I cannot die here.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.52,0:16:39.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.46,0:16:42.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Fate won, and you are the loser.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.96,0:16:44.66,Default,,0,0,0,,You insignificant little.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.88,0:16:46.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't do this alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.30,0:16:50.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene knew I'd make it here, and this\Nis what she would've wanted me to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.92,0:16:56.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Brother 2, and FF, Ermes,\NAnastasia, and even Mr. Jotaro.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.74,0:17:01.51,Default,,0,0,0,,We had no idea what the future\Nheld, but we all had resolutions.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.88,0:17:05.41,Default,,0,0,0,,The one who couldn't accept\Ntheir own fate was you, Poochie.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.96,0:17:08.67,Default,,0,0,0,,True fate is walking\Ndown the path of justice.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.80,0:17:09.80,Default,,0,0,0,,You're done for!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.02,0:17:11.42,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I'm not!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.46,0:17:15.23,Default,,0,0,0,,You're the one who doesn't\Nunderstand anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.36,0:17:20.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Go to hell, you insignificant little brat!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.34,0:18:02.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my God.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.64,0:18:26.47,Default,,0,0,0,,The bus
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.94,0:18:32.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Give me a break. I already told\Nyou I've only got this 50 on me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.48,0:18:36.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Why don't you carry\Nchange on the bus anyway
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.32,0:18:42.98,Default,,0,0,0,,You're for real. You gotta top down.\NFine. Fine. Just hold up a sec.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.06,0:18:46.94,Default,,0,0,0,,would ya I'm gonna go break this\N50 at that gas station real quick
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.16,0:18:49.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, hey kid, you gettin' on this bus?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.52,0:18:51.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Talk about perfect timing.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.46,0:18:52.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You got any change?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.04,0:18:54.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I need to break this 50.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.20,0:18:56.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.11,0:18:56.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that good with you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.06,0:18:59.00,Default,,0,0,0,,It ain't a counterfeit, trust me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.52,0:19:00.35,Default,,0,0,0,,What the?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.43,0:19:02.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't leave me, dumbass!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.36,0:19:04.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, just throw it back like that!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.10,0:19:04.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.26,0:19:07.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.30,0:19:10.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The bus went and drove off because your\Nresponse time was so freakin' slow!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.04,0:19:13.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna wait two hours for the next one.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.18,0:19:14.06,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell, man?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.14,0:19:14.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Ben!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.05,0:19:16.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you even listening to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.76,0:19:17.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.24,0:19:19.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, well, whatever.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.76,0:19:23.46,Default,,0,0,0,,That cheap prick probably thought I was a\Nfugitive from Green Dolphin or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.54,0:19:24.37,Default,,0,0,0,,You...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.45,0:19:25.28,Default,,0,0,0,,you are?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.90,0:19:26.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.38,0:19:29.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.29,0:19:30.90,Default,,0,0,0,,My car completely ran out of gas.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.40,0:19:34.22,Default,,0,0,0,,If you hook us up with some\Ngas and food with that 50,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.30,0:19:37.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll let you catch a ride\Nto wherever you want to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.42,0:19:38.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Same goes for you, kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.58,0:19:42.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that how you save on\Ntravel expenses or something?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.14,0:19:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,My sister used to always tell me to never\Nget in a car with some random stranger.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.66,0:19:56.02,Default,,0,0,0,,There's a storm on the way.\NToo bad, have fun getting.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.10,0:19:58.78,Default,,0,0,0,,drenched while you wait\Nfor the next bus to come!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.86,0:20:01.63,Default,,0,0,0,,But I don't think it's\Nletting up anytime soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.04,0:20:10.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Hop on in, kiddo.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.80,0:20:12.68,Default,,0,0,0,,It's okay, we're not bad people.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.86,0:20:18.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Call me Irene, and this\Nguy here is Anikis.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.68,0:20:20.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's your mom and dad at, bud?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.76,0:20:24.47,Default,,0,0,0,,We were actually just on our way\Nto visit my old man right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.42,0:20:27.25,Default,,0,0,0,,You see?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.16,0:20:29.28,Default,,0,0,0,,He's my boyfriend.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.16,0:20:36.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know how things will turn out,\Nbut if Dad approves of us being together,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.52,0:20:39.30,Default,,0,0,0,,then maybe we'll even get married.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.80,0:20:42.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.98,0:20:44.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Is there really a storm heading this way?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.00,0:20:48.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll ride along, but ten bucks\Nis all you're getting from me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.08,0:20:51.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna have you guys make a\Nstop at Cape Canaveral, too, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.44,0:20:52.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, get in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.68,0:20:54.45,Default,,0,0,0,,We could really use your help.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.62,0:20:56.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, me too. To be honest.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.32,0:20:59.26,Default,,0,0,0,,You doing okay there, little boy?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.88,0:21:02.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you tell me your name?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.52,0:21:07.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, I said to get in.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.22,0:21:13.57,Default,,0,0,0,,And I don't expect you to pay us either.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.36,0:21:15.95,Default,,0,0,0,,You're shaking like a tree.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.56,0:21:17.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you cold?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.46,0:21:19.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.10,0:21:23.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Emporio.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.02,0:21:27.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Emporio.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.54,0:21:36.34,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what you can call me, since\Nyou wanted to know my name's Emporio.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.38,0:21:51.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, look, there's a hitchhiker.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.96,0:21:54.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not picking up another straggler.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.28,0:21:55.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Two is more than enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.70,0:21:58.32,Default,,0,0,0,,You're the one that said\Nthere's a storm coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.40,0:22:00.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, stop the car for the poor guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.10,0:22:25.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be the roundabout.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.02,0:22:30.10,Default,,0,0,0,,The words will make you out and out.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.18,0:22:33.40,Default,,0,0,0,,And spend the day your way.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.30,0:22:38.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Call it morning driving through the sun.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.28,0:22:39.88,Default,,0,0,0,,And in and out the valley.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.32,0:22:52.98,Default,,0,0,0,,The music dance and sing.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.06,0:22:57.14,Default,,0,0,0,,They make the children really ring.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.22,0:23:01.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I spend the day your way.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.54,0:23:05.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Cold and morning, driving through the sun.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.42,0:23:07.14,Default,,0,0,0,,And in and out the valley.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.08,0:23:11.78,Default,,0,0,0,,In and out around the lake.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.86,0:23:15.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Mountains come out of the sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.28,0:23:16.94,Default,,0,0,0,,And they stand there.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.98,0:23:23.66,Default,,0,0,0,,When my lover will be\Nthere and we'll see you.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.42,0:23:30.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Ten and two summers will\Nbe there laughing too.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.98,0:23:35.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Twenty and four before my lover will see.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.82,0:23:38.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be there with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:16.94,0:24:21.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
